  "claim": "Sully is the nickname of this American retired airline captain celebrated for his water landing with Jeffrey Skiles, after a bird strike and being unable to reach an airport.",
  "evidencia": "Page: US Airways Flight 1549. Sentence: US Airways Flight 1549 was an Airbus A320-214 which, three minutes after takeoff from New York City's LaGuardia Airport on January 15, 2009, struck a flock of Canada geese just northeast of the George Washington Bridge and consequently lost all engine power.\nPage: US Airways Flight 1549. Sentence: Unable to reach any airport, pilots Chesley Sullenberger and Jeffrey Skiles glided the plane to a ditching in the Hudson River off Midtown Manhattan.\nPage: Chesley Sullenberger. Sentence: Chesley Burnett \"Sully\" Sullenberger III (born 1951) is an American retired airline captain celebrated for the January 15, 2009 water landing of US Airways Flight 1549 in the Hudson River off Manhattan after the plane was disabled by striking a flock of Canada geese immediately after takeoff; all 155 people aboard survived.",
